sed
Usage: sed [-i[SFX]] [-nrE] [-f FILE]... [-e CMD]... [FILE]...
or: sed [-i[SFX]] [-nrE] CMD [FILE]...

Filter and transform text using scripted edit commands.

	-e CMD	Add CMD to sed commands to be executed
	-f FILE	Add FILE contents to sed commands to be executed
	-i[SFX]	Edit files in-place (otherwise write to stdout)
		Optionally back files up, appending SFX
	-n	Only print lines you explicitly print (with p)
	-r,-E	Use extended regex syntax

If no -e or -f, the first non-option argument is the sed command string.
Remaining arguments are input files (stdin if none).

Script commands:
	s/RE/REPL/FLAGS	Replace matches of RE with REPL
			FLAGS: g (all matches), I (ignore case), p (print)
	p		Print the current line
	d		Delete the current line
Addresses (before a command, select which lines it runs on):
	N		Line number N
	$		The last line
	/RE/		Any line matching RE
	N,M		Lines N through M
